    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1ae5cdf2_0d5b3355",
        "filename": "keystone/auth/plugins/oidc.py",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 120,
      "author": {
        "id": 8978
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-05-30T08:57:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please, do. I think it\u0027s extremely important to clarify on this.\nOtherwise we will get tons of compaints from security teams.\n\nAlso, since openid itself doesn\u0027t specify that user should authenticate via http basicauth I can easily imagine an idp enforcing x509 authn.",
      "parentUuid": "3ae8d1ca_981ba61a",
      "revId": "9be8b648fffe0049d5f750c0b90d65a5b4683309",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3ae8d1ca_fcf2ec98",
        "filename": "keystone/auth/plugins/oidc.py",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 131,
      "author": {
        "id": 8978
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-05-29T07:49:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "By setting auth\u003duser_auth you assume the Http Basic Auth method will be used.\nI don\u0027t think this is a right assumption unless openid spec specifies that. If it does, please paste a link for that spec.",
      "revId": "9be8b648fffe0049d5f750c0b90d65a5b4683309",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3ae8d1ca_f8a58ab5",
        "filename": "keystone/auth/plugins/oidc.py",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 131,
      "author": {
        "id": 6482
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-05-29T16:28:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, I\u0027m re-reading the spec now and it says that the auth method used is out of the scope of the spec. So I\u0027m wondering what about other auth methods (session cookie or token)...",
      "parentUuid": "3ae8d1ca_fcf2ec98",
      "revId": "9be8b648fffe0049d5f750c0b90d65a5b4683309",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1ae5cdf2_9052f811",
        "filename": "keystone/auth/plugins/oidc.py",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 131,
      "author": {
        "id": 8978
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-05-30T08:57:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I suspect the story is just like in SAML world - it\u0027s up to IdP (or however you call it in openid) admins how their users will authenticate - it can be basicauth, x509 certificate, and almost everything. I think what we should do is to let Keystone use many authn methods, by creating a pluggable mechanism. This is how I want to make it work for SAML in python-keystoneclient (and I strongly believe this part for openid should also be moved to keystoneclient).",
      "parentUuid": "3ae8d1ca_f8a58ab5",
      "revId": "9be8b648fffe0049d5f750c0b90d65a5b4683309",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
